              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Richard S. Huszagh), it is unquestionably fraudulent to induce a donation by claiming a specific charitable purpose when, in fact, only a nominal amount goes to that purpose and the solicitor keeps the vast majority."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Illinois Attorney General)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
