              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5dc8d6195520-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondents (Mr. Copilevitz), charities\u2019 decisions about how much to spend on fundraising are a measure of judgment, constitute protected speech, and cannot be second\u2011guessed."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Defendants",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5dc8d619552069c29a1804baed87c00b4e13246086d0b11fa2d5aca8e0b96eed",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5dc8d6195520-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Defendants argue that unless there is an explicit factual misrepresentation, they should receive blanket immunity from liability for charitable fundraising claims."
        }
      ],
